["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG7aa084bf85f669cdfffaa28421937f6dd10ec63ce76aad5b3adee5fd7e5603bd","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/canonical-command-retries","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nVersion 1 already decides that realm, workspace, authority and key identify a retry. The existing memory and entity adapters persist only command id and result, so different intent can currently be mistaken for a replay.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA stored applied command carries canonical caller-controlled intent, equal intent returns the original result across executors of one authority, different intent is refused by name, and legacy intent-less records never replay as though equivalence had been proven.\n\n## Implementation\n\nCommand idempotency now persists canonical `CommandIntent`: caller-controlled command type, payload, realm, workspace, authority, and key, excluding executor identity. Equal intent returns the original result across executors of one authority; different intent is refused as an idempotency conflict; legacy records without intent cannot be treated as proven replay equivalence. Memory and entity-backed tests cover all three cases.\n","relations":[{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Make durable replay depend on caller-controlled intent rather than command identity alone.","title":"Compare canonical intent for scoped command retries"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG7aa084bf85f669cdfffaa28421937f6dd10ec63ce76aad5b3adee5fd7e5603bd","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG7aa084bf85f669cdfffaa28421937f6dd10ec63ce76aad5b3adee5fd7e5603bd"]}]